## Realistic Signature Buildings
Build the city you want, without making the economy unrealistically easy.
Place multiple Unique and Signature buildings for their appearance, while controlling how their bonuses stack. Or keep the original vanilla effects—it's your choice.


### All Optional:
- Place as many Unique buildings as you want without stacking their bonuses.
- Unlock all Signature buildings, build extra copies, and choose exactly which effects they provide.
- City wide effects and local effects can be control separately.
Example, if you don't want double stacked 10% + 10% bonus to all city becausee you placed two of the same building, but you still want the small area effect for happiness near the buildings, you can do that.

### Signature bonuses: two independent controls

**City-wide Signature bonuses** (default: First copy only)
- **First copy only** — each Signature building type provides its city-wide bonus once, even if you build more copies.
- **No city-wide bonuses** — disables Signature city-wide bonuses.
- **Vanilla Stacked Bonuses** — every placed copy provides its normal city-wide bonus.

**Nearby Signature effects** (default: Vanilla nearby effects)
- **Vanilla nearby effects** — every copy provides its normal local effects.
- **First copy only** — one copy of each Signature building type provides local effects.
- **No nearby effects** — disables normal local effects from Signature buildings.

These controls work independently. Building attractiveness and abandoned-building effects are not removed.

### More features
- **Unlock Signature requirements** — make Signature buildings available without population, zoning, or other progression requirements (default: OFF).
- **Allow multiple copies of Unique buildings**, including Signatures (default: ON). Switching this OFF does not bulldoze copies already placed.
- **Live Options** — bonus modes change without restarting the city.
- **Status and diagnostics** — view the number of Signature buildings, duplicates, and active city-wide bonus providers. Use **Bonus Report to log** and **Nearby Report to log** to test modes and restore your chosen settings.
- Works alongside **Anarchy**. Other mods with the same Multiple Unique feature are redundant.

### Notes
- No Harmony patching.
- Most changes happen when needed; no ongoing city-wide scanning for the bonus dropdowns.
- To read diagnostic results: Options > About > Debug / Logging > Open Log.
- Hover over Options rows for explanations.
- Custom assets may have different bonus types or none at all.

### Languages
English, Français, Deutsch, Español, Italiano, Polski, Português (Brasil), Português (Portugal), Türkçe, ไทย, Tiếng Việt, 日本語, 한국어, 简体中文, 繁體中文

### Credits and feedback
